;; Two post mills on the crater floor (issue #61), each taking the map's wind where it stands:
;; one on the line from the rim's notch (azimuth 200) through the centre, where the corridor
;; is strongest, one 160 m across it, where the wind is the corridor's base 0.3 of that. The
;; same mill; a very different wind, and a power that goes as its cube.
(world crater-wind
  (map victoria)
  (place in-corridor field-windmill (at -94.0 0 -34.2))
  (place off-corridor field-windmill (at 54.7 0 -150.4)))
